Declarations are read as whole statements, so a comma list broken across
lines and a bare :DECLARE with its names on later lines still declare
every name (diag.undeclared_variable near-miss). Nothing fires under any
profile; every name is also used, so diag.unused_variable stays quiet.
(A leading-comma continuation, `, sSuffix;` on its own line, was dropped
from this input: range-formatting the line before it appends a `;`.)
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE JoinLabels;
	:PARAMETERS sPrefix, sStem,
		sSuffix;
	:DECLARE
		sJoined,
		sSeparator;
	sSeparator := "-";
	sJoined := sPrefix + sSeparator + sStem + sSeparator + sSuffix;
	:RETURN sJoined;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE JoinLabels;
	:PARAMETERS sPrefix, sStem,
	            sSuffix;
	:DECLARE
	sJoined,
		sSeparator;
	sSeparator := "-";
	sJoined := sPrefix + sSeparator + sStem + sSeparator + sSuffix;
	:RETURN sJoined;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
